<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Morgan denies EMU delay rumour.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Morgan denies EMU delay rumour.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman for Deutsche Morgan Grenfell denied talk in foreign exchange markets that the investment house raised the possibility of delay in European monetary union with its customers.</p>
<p>&quot;This talk is totally without basis,&quot; the spokesman said, adding such speculation was counter-productive.</p>
<p>Rumours that Deutsche Morgan Grenfell had raised the possibility of an EMU delay lifted the mark against the dollar earlier in the day.  </p>
<p>London currency dealers reported talk that the bank had raised the possibility of a delay to EMU with its customers.</p>
<p>The new single European currency is due to be launched in January 1999.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
